  "category" : "crafting",
  "level" : 6, "race" : "alta",

  "shortdescription" : "^orange;Alta Armory^reset;",
  "description" : "An ^#b0e0fc;alta^reset; military crafting station for producing ^#60c0fc;armor^reset;, ^#60c0fc;shields^reset;, and defensive equipment.",
  "longdescription" : "The Alta Armory is a tier 6 military equipment fabrication station specialized in defensive technology. This fortress-grade workshop produces ^#60c0fc;combat armor sets^reset; with integrated energy shields, ^#60c0fc;EPP modules^reset; with environmental protection, defensive ^#60c0fc;augments^reset; for enhanced survivability, and various ^#60c0fc;shield generators^reset; and protective devices. The station features armor plating forges, shield field calibration equipment, and ^#60c0fc;bion compound^reset; integration systems. While altas prefer peaceful solutions, the Armory ensures they're well-protected when danger is unavoidable.",
  "altaDescription" : "The defense equipment station! We may prefer peace, but when exploration gets dangerous, proper armor and shields are essential for survival~",

  "apexDescription" : "Alta defensive technology workshop. Their energy shield integration is highly sophisticated.",
  "avianDescription" : "A forge for protective armor! Even peaceful explorers need good defense sometimes.",
  "floranDescription" : "Makesss armor and shieldsss. Floran likesss offenssse more but defenssse good too.",
  "glitchDescription" : "Approving. This station demonstrates that altas value protection over aggression.",
  "humanDescription" : "Armor workshop! Shields, EPPs, defensive augments - full protection suite.",
  "hylotlDescription" : "A station dedicated to defense rather than offense. The alta philosophy of protection resonates deeply.",
  "novakidDescription" : "Armor makin' station! Shields and protective gear for when things get rough out there.",

  "inventoryIcon" : "icon.png",
  "orientations" : [
    { "dualImage" : "body.png", "spaceScan" : 0.1, "anchors" : [ "bottom" ], "collision" : "platform" }
  ],

